{
 "hash": "159a154e6a187b",
 "text": "In my world, the toaster burns the last thing you say onto your toast. I'm Maya. I'm a terrible liar. And this morning... I broke Mum's favourite mug. Everyone is scared of that toaster. Last night, Mum told me my drawing was amazing. Then she muttered something at the fridge. This morning, her toast said... weird dog. She ate it before anyone could read it. Mum reads everyone's toast out loud, at seven. Hers always says, good morning. She says it to the toaster every night. Ten years, perfect toast. She is very proud. It was six fifty-eight. My secret? I whisper sorry to the toaster. Every morning. Out loud. For practice. Mum thinks it's silly. But it's the only way I can say sorry without my voice shaking. Then Mum found the mug. She held up the pieces. Maya, did you break this? I panicked. I said: I did not break your mug. Mum dropped bread in the toaster and said, let's see what it says. Thirty seconds. And my lie was the last thing I'd said. But the toaster burns the last thing you say. Not the first thing. The last. So I kept talking. I whispered my practised sorry. Every word. Out loud. To Mum. The toast popped. It said: sorry Mum, it was me. Mum read it twice. Then she walked to the toaster. Dropped in her own bread. And whispered, very quietly, the one thing she had never said out loud. Her toast said: I love the weird dog.",
 "voice": "georgeHushed",
